-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ב/7 (17.7.2022): קצובת ביגוד לשנת הלימודים תשפ"ב, קצובת
-- ביגוד לעובדי הוראה בחינוך הגופני, קצובת ביגוד לעובדי הוראה בחינוך הטכנולוגי.
-- The clothing allowance for the school year תשפ"ב (who, how much, when, and
-- part-time and multiple employers), the additional allowance of physical-
-- education teachers by position, and the allowance of technological-
-- education staff by profession.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `תשפ"ב/7 קצובת ביגוד לשנת הלימודים תשפ"ב`

-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 The letterhead in Hebrew and Arabic, its address line and privacy notice; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 akn:preamble/p13 akn:preamble/p14 akn:preamble/p15 The date, the reference number, the addressees, the greeting and the subject line; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p16 akn:preamble/p17 akn:preamble/p18 The circular's list of its three subjects, each encoded below; no rule.

-- Time in the regulative rules is counted in school months (common.l4:
-- September is 1, so July is 11).

DECLARE `clothing action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the clothing allowance` HAS `clothing amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the physical-education allowance` HAS `physical-education amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the technological-education allowance` HAS `technological amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `work at a total position with all employers` HAS `track worked` IS AN `employment track`, `total position worked` IS A NUMBER, `work permitted by the procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employ at a total position with all employers` HAS `track employed` IS AN `employment track`, `total position employed` IS A NUMBER, `employment permitted by the procedure` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `1 קצובת ביגוד לשנת הלימודים תשפ"ב`

-- akn:art_1/p1 The heading "תחולה" (scope); no rule.
-- akn:art_1/p4 The heading "כללי" (general); no rule.

@desc A teaching employee as far as the clothing allowance asks about it.
DECLARE `clothing employee` HAS
    `rated on the teaching-employee scale`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by an owner of a supervised institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed by an owner of education the Ministry of Education supervises
    `position fraction at the paying employer`         IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position held with the employer that pays (1 = one full position)

-- ¶2: who the section applies to; ¶3: it follows the Treasury's
-- instructions on the clothing allowance.
@ref akn:art_1/p2 akn:art_1/p3
GIVEN e IS A `clothing employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1 applies to` e IF
        e's `rated on the teaching-employee scale`
    AND e's `employed by an owner of a supervised institution`

-- §1ב: entitled as civil servants who receive the public are, for the
-- school year תשפ"ב (9/21-8/22); §1ג: at level 4, ₪2,237.
@ref akn:art_1__para_b
GIVEN e IS A `clothing employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the clothing allowance for תשפ"ב` e IF
    `section 1 applies to` e

@ref akn:art_1__para_c
`the clothing allowance at level 4` MEANS 2237

-- §1ד: in proportion to the position, up to one full position (100%).
-- §1ה: with more than one employer and more than 100% in all, each employer
-- pays in proportion to the position held with it — which is what §1ד
-- already gives each employer, the cap being per employer.
@ref akn:art_1__para_d akn:art_1__para_e
GIVEN e IS A `clothing employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the clothing allowance owed by the employer` e IS
    IF `entitled to the clothing allowance for תשפ"ב` e
    THEN `the clothing allowance at level 4` TIMES min (e's `position fraction at the paying employer`) 1
    ELSE 0

-- §1א: paid in full with July 2022's salary.
@ref akn:art_1__para_a
GIVEN e IS A `clothing employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `paying the clothing allowance with July's salary` e IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the clothing allowance` paid
          PROVIDED paid AT LEAST `the clothing allowance owed by the employer` e
    WITHIN `month number` July
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תשפ\"ב/7 §1א: the clothing allowance is paid in full with July 2022's salary"

-- §1ו: the limits on total employment with all employers. ¶1's first
-- limit is on every teaching employee: 140%.
@ref akn:art_1__para_f
`the limit on every teaching employee` MEANS 1.40

-- ¶1's second limit and ¶2's: the limit by track.
@ref akn:art_1__para_f akn:art_1__para_f/p2
GIVEN t IS AN `employment track`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the limit section 1ו sets for the track` t IS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `a principal not employed under a reform` THEN 1.50
    WHEN `a teacher under Oz LaTmura in full implementation` THEN 1.25
    WHEN `a teacher under Ofek Hadash` THEN 1.17
    OTHERWISE `the limit on every teaching employee`

@desc The employment tracks section 1ו names.
DECLARE `employment track` IS ONE OF
    `a teaching employee not employed under a reform`
    `a principal not employed under a reform`
    `a teacher under Oz LaTmura in full implementation`
    `a teacher under Ofek Hadash`

-- ¶5 restates the limits by reform only.
@ref akn:art_1/p5
GIVEN t IS AN `employment track`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the limit as ¶5 restates it` t IS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `a teacher under Oz LaTmura in full implementation` THEN 1.25
    WHEN `a teacher under Ofek Hadash` THEN 1.17
    OTHERWISE 1.40

-- F-2021-22_tashpab_07-a: a principal outside the reforms is a teaching
-- employee, so §1ו limits the same employment at 140% and at 150%, and ¶5
-- repeats 140%.
`a principal outside the reforms is given two limits` MEANS
        NOT (`the limit section 1ו sets for the track` `a principal not employed under a reform` EQUALS `the limit on every teaching employee`)
    AND `the limit as ¶5 restates it` `a principal not employed under a reform` EQUALS `the limit on every teaching employee`
#ASSERT `a principal outside the reforms is given two limits`

-- The reading adopted: the specific limit governs the track it names, so a
-- principal outside the reforms may work up to 150%. ¶3-4: subject to the
-- exceptional-employment procedure for תשפ"ב (an input).
@ref akn:art_1__para_f/p3 akn:art_1__para_f/p4
GIVEN t IS AN `employment track`
      `total position with all employers` IS A NUMBER
      `permitted under the exceptional-employment procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc whether the exceptional-employment procedure for תשפ"ב permits this employment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employment is within the limits` t `total position with all employers` `permitted under the exceptional-employment procedure` IF
        `total position with all employers` AT MOST `the limit section 1ו sets for the track` t
    OR  `permitted under the exceptional-employment procedure`

-- §1ו ¶1 puts the limit on the employee ("הגבלה על עובד הוראה לעבוד"), ¶2
-- on the employment ("העסקתו ... מוגבלת", ¶5 "היתר להעסקה"): both are
-- bound. The exception is the exceptional-employment procedure (¶3). The
-- text sets no time limit, so neither prohibition has one.
@ref akn:art_1__para_f akn:art_1/p5
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `no employment beyond the limits` IS
    (PARTY `the teaching employee`
     SHANT `work at a total position with all employers` t total permitted
           PROVIDED NOT `the employment is within the limits` t total permitted
     LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "תשפ\"ב/7 §1ו: a teaching employee does not work beyond the limit on total employment unless the exceptional-employment procedure permits it")
    RAND
    (PARTY `the employer`
     SHANT `employ at a total position with all employers` t total permitted
           PROVIDED NOT `the employment is within the limits` t total permitted
     LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תשפ\"ב/7 §1ו: employment beyond the limit on total employment needs the exceptional-employment procedure; the circular changes nothing in it")

§§ `2 קצובת ביגוד נוספת למורה לחינוך גופני`

-- ¶1: in addition to the general allowance (and covering sun-protection
-- products). ¶2: the amounts of circular תשע"ב/8 are updated by the table.
@desc One printed row of section 2's table: a band of the position and its amount as at 1.9.2021.
DECLARE `PE band` HAS
    `band lowest fraction`           IS A NUMBER
    `lowest fraction included`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `band highest fraction`          IS A NUMBER
    `highest fraction included`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `PE amount`                      IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_2/p2 akn:art_2/t1
`the physical-education table` MEANS
    LIST `PE band` 0       TRUE  (1 DIVIDED BY 3) FALSE 0,
         `PE band` (1 DIVIDED BY 3) TRUE 0.5     TRUE  714,
         `PE band` 0.5     FALSE 999     TRUE  1423

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER, b IS A `PE band`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the band holds` f b IF
        (f GREATER THAN b's `band lowest fraction` OR (b's `lowest fraction included` AND f EQUALS b's `band lowest fraction`))
    AND (f LESS THAN b's `band highest fraction` OR (b's `highest fraction included` AND f EQUALS b's `band highest fraction`))

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the amounts the table gives for` f IS
    map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `PE amount`) (filter (GIVEN b YIELD `the band holds` f b) `the physical-education table`)

-- Every position from 0 to 1.5, in steps of a twelfth and at a third and a
-- half exactly, falls in exactly one band.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD count (`the amounts the table gives for` f) EQUALS 1)
            (map (GIVEN n YIELD n DIVIDED BY 12) (range 0 18))

-- F-2021-22_tashpab_07-b: the table bands "שיעור העסקה" without saying
-- whether that is the position with one employer or with all of them. The
-- reading adopted: the position with the paying employer, each employer
-- paying its own band (as §1ה does for the general allowance).
-- F-2021-22_tashpab_07-e: "שיעור העסקה" is not said to be the share of the position in
-- physical education or the employee's whole position. The reading
-- adopted, as F-2019-20_tashaf_11-c and its siblings read the same words:
-- the share in physical education, as the input below is named.
GIVEN `position as a physical-education teacher` IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a full position held as a physical-education teacher with the paying employer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the additional physical-education allowance` `position as a physical-education teacher` IS
    sum (`the amounts the table gives for` `position as a physical-education teacher`)

`the two readings of the employment rate differ` MEANS
    NOT (`the amounts the table gives for` 0.2 EQUALS `the amounts the table gives for` 1)
#ASSERT `the two readings of the employment rate differ`

-- F-2021-22_tashpab_07-f: no month is printed for the physical-education or the
-- technological-education allowance; §1א's July is under section 1's own
-- heading. The reading adopted, as F-2019-20_tashaf_11-d: the extras are
-- paid with the general allowance, with the July 2022 salary.
GIVEN `position as a physical-education teacher` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `paying the physical-education allowance with July's salary` `position as a physical-education teacher` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the physical-education allowance` paid
          PROVIDED paid AT LEAST `the additional physical-education allowance` `position as a physical-education teacher`
    WITHIN `month number` July
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תשפ\"ב/7 §2: the extra allowance is paid with the general allowance, in July 2022"

DECLARE `section of the circular` IS ONE OF `section 1`, `section 2`, `section 3`
GIVEN x IS A `section of the circular`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `names a payment month` x IF
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `section 1` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

`sections 2 and 3 name no payment month` MEANS
    (NOT `names a payment month` `section 2`) AND NOT `names a payment month` `section 3`
#ASSERT `sections 2 and 3 name no payment month`

`two employers at 40% each pay more than one employer at 80%` MEANS
    `the additional physical-education allowance` 0.4 PLUS `the additional physical-education allowance` 0.4
        GREATER THAN `the additional physical-education allowance` 0.8
#ASSERT `two employers at 40% each pay more than one employer at 80%`

-- ¶1: the allowance is in addition to the clothing allowance of all
-- teaching employees (and covers sun-protection products).
@ref akn:art_2/p1
GIVEN e IS A `clothing employee`
      `position as a physical-education teacher` IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a full position held as a physical-education teacher with the paying employer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the clothing allowances of a physical-education teacher` e `position as a physical-education teacher` IS
    `the clothing allowance owed by the employer` e
        PLUS `the additional physical-education allowance` `position as a physical-education teacher`

§§ `3 קצובת ביגוד בחינוך הטכנולוגי`

@desc The professions of section 3's two lists, in the printed order.
DECLARE `technological profession` IS ONE OF
    `aviation systems`
    `mechatronics`
    `marine technical thermodynamics`
    `CAD-CAM systems`
    `maintenance of mechanical systems`
    `automotive mechanics systems`
    `computerised automotive systems`
    `power, command and control systems`
    `climate-control systems`
    `hotel cooking and baking`
    `seamanship - ships`
    `television and cinema systems`
    `photography systems`
    `electronic systems`
    `computing and control systems`
    `computer systems`
    `systems design and programming`
    `biotechnology systems`
    `tourism management`
    `hotel management`
    `early childhood education`
    `design`
    `fashion and costume`
    `hairdressing and beauty care`
    `nursing`
    `applied art`
    `another profession`

-- §3.1א: shoes and two robes a year, worth ₪589.
@ref akn:art_3__para_1__subpara_a akn:art_3__para_1__subpara_a/t1
`the shoes-and-robes professions` MEANS
    LIST `aviation systems`, `mechatronics`, `marine technical thermodynamics`,
         `CAD-CAM systems`, `maintenance of mechanical systems`,
         `automotive mechanics systems`, `computerised automotive systems`,
         `power, command and control systems`, `climate-control systems`,
         `hotel cooking and baking`, `seamanship - ships`,
         `television and cinema systems`, `photography systems`

@ref akn:art_3__para_1__subpara_a/p2
`the value of shoes and two robes` MEANS 589

-- §3.1ב: two robes a year, worth ₪366.
@ref akn:art_3__para_1__subpara_b akn:art_3__para_1__subpara_b/t1
`the two-robes professions` MEANS
    LIST `electronic systems`, `computing and control systems`, `computer systems`,
         `systems design and programming`, `biotechnology systems`,
         `tourism management`, `hotel management`, `early childhood education`,
         `design`, `fashion and costume`, `hairdressing and beauty care`,
         `nursing`, `applied art`

@ref akn:art_3__para_1__subpara_b/p2
`the value of two robes` MEANS 366

-- The two lists name no profession twice.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN p YIELD NOT elem p `the two-robes professions`) `the shoes-and-robes professions`

-- ¶1: payable to a teaching employee in technological education or a
-- vocational instructor, by the profession taught. §3.3: in proportion to
-- the position in technological education, up to one full position.
@ref akn:art_3/p1 akn:art_3__para_3
GIVEN p IS A `technological profession`
      `position in technological education` IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a full position in technological education (1 = one full position)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the technological-education clothing allowance` p `position in technological education` IS
    `the full value for the profession` p TIMES min `position in technological education` 1

GIVEN p IS A `technological profession`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full value for the profession` p IS
    IF elem p `the shoes-and-robes professions`
    THEN `the value of shoes and two robes`
    ELSE IF elem p `the two-robes professions`
         THEN `the value of two robes`
         ELSE 0

-- F-2021-22_tashpab_07-d: a teacher of professions on both lists is given the shoes and
-- robes AND the robes by the words; the reading adopted, as
-- F-2019-20_tashaf_11-b: the higher item, once, pro rata.
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `technological profession`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the items the lists give` ps IS
    append (IF any (GIVEN p YIELD elem p `the shoes-and-robes professions`) ps THEN LIST `the value of shoes and two robes` ELSE EMPTY)
           (IF any (GIVEN p YIELD elem p `the two-robes professions`) ps THEN LIST `the value of two robes` ELSE EMPTY)

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `technological profession`
      `position in technological education` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the technological-education allowance for the professions taught` ps `position in technological education` IS
    CONSIDER `the items the lists give` ps
    WHEN a FOLLOWED BY rest THEN a TIMES min `position in technological education` 1
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0

`a teacher of subjects on both lists is given two items` MEANS
    `the items the lists give` (LIST `mechatronics`, `nursing`) EQUALS LIST 589, 366
#ASSERT `a teacher of subjects on both lists is given two items`
#ASSERT `the technological-education allowance for the professions taught` (LIST `mechatronics`, `nursing`) 1 EQUALS 589

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `technological profession`
      `position in technological education` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `paying the technological-education allowance with July's salary` ps `position in technological education` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the technological-education allowance` paid
          PROVIDED paid AT LEAST `the technological-education allowance for the professions taught` ps `position in technological education`
    WITHIN `month number` July
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "תשפ\"ב/7 §3: the technological allowance is paid with the general allowance, in July 2022"

-- §3.2: the allowance is in addition to the clothing allowance of all
-- teaching employees.
@ref akn:art_3__para_2
GIVEN e IS A `clothing employee`
      p IS A `technological profession`
      `position in technological education` IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a full position in technological education (1 = one full position)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the clothing allowances of a technological-education employee` e p `position in technological education` IS
    `the clothing allowance owed by the employer` e
        PLUS `the technological-education clothing allowance` p `position in technological education`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: the telephone numbers for questions, the signatures and the list of copies; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

`a full-time teacher` MEANS `clothing employee` TRUE TRUE 1
`a teacher at 120% with one employer` MEANS `clothing employee` TRUE TRUE 1.2
`a teacher at 60%` MEANS `clothing employee` TRUE TRUE 0.6

#ASSERT `the clothing allowance owed by the employer` `a full-time teacher` EQUALS 2237
#ASSERT `the clothing allowance owed by the employer` `a teacher at 120% with one employer` EQUALS 2237
#ASSERT `the clothing allowance owed by the employer` `a teacher at 60%` EQUALS 1342.2
#ASSERT `the additional physical-education allowance` (1 DIVIDED BY 3) EQUALS 714
#ASSERT `the additional physical-education allowance` 0.3 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the additional physical-education allowance` 0.75 EQUALS 1423
#ASSERT `the technological-education clothing allowance` `mechatronics` 0.5 EQUALS 294.5
#ASSERT `the technological-education clothing allowance` `nursing` 1.3 EQUALS 366
#ASSERT `the employment is within the limits` `a principal not employed under a reform` 1.45 FALSE

#TRACE `paying the clothing allowance with July's salary` `a full-time teacher` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the clothing allowance` 2237 AT 11

#ASSERT `the clothing allowances of a physical-education teacher` `a full-time teacher` 0.75 EQUALS 3660
#ASSERT `the clothing allowances of a technological-education employee` `a full-time teacher` `nursing` 1 EQUALS 2603

#TRACE `no employment beyond the limits` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `employ at a total position with all employers` `a teacher under Ofek Hadash` 1.2 FALSE AT 1

-- F-2021-22_tashpab_07-c: §1ד pays by the position "and not more than one full
-- position"; §1ה pays an employee of several employers, whose total is
-- above 100%, each employer's own share. Reading adopted, as in
-- F-2018-19_tashat_08-b: §1ה governs several employers, and §1ד's cap is
-- at each employer, as the allowance above is encoded.
`the employer shares the multi-employer rule gives for 80% and 60%` MEANS LIST 0.8, 0.6
`the one-position cap and the multi-employer rule disagree for two employers` MEANS
    sum `the employer shares the multi-employer rule gives for 80% and 60%` GREATER THAN 1
#ASSERT `the one-position cap and the multi-employer rule disagree for two employers`

§§ `Property checks`

-- The circular over a finite space: covered or not; positions and physical-
-- education shares in tenths from 0 to 1.5, with a third and a half; one
-- profession from each list, both, or none; every track of employment;
-- total positions in tenths, permitted by the procedure or not.

`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE
`tenths to 1.5` MEANS map (GIVEN k YIELD k DIVIDED BY 10) (range 0 15)
`the shares checked` MEANS append `tenths to 1.5` (LIST 1 DIVIDED BY 3, 0.3333, 0.5001)
`every profession list checked` MEANS
    LIST EMPTY, (LIST `mechatronics`), (LIST `nursing`), (LIST `another profession`), (LIST `mechatronics`, `nursing`)
`every track` MEANS LIST `a teaching employee not employed under a reform`, `a principal not employed under a reform`, `a teacher under Oz LaTmura in full implementation`, `a teacher under Ofek Hadash`

-- §1 over coverage and position: level 4 pro rata to the position up to
-- one, nothing outside the circular, never falling with a larger position.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD
                all (GIVEN f YIELD
                        LET a MEANS `the clothing allowance owed by the employer` (`clothing employee` r TRUE f)
                        IN      a EQUALS (IF r THEN 2237 TIMES min f 1 ELSE 0)
                            AND a AT MOST `the clothing allowance owed by the employer` (`clothing employee` r TRUE (f PLUS 0.1)))
                    `tenths to 1.5`)
            `both booleans`

-- §1ו over every track and total position: within the limits exactly up
-- to the track's limit or with the procedure's permission; the principal's
-- 150% (finding a's reading) is the highest limit.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD
                all (GIVEN k YIELD
                        all (GIVEN pm YIELD
                                    `the employment is within the limits` t (k DIVIDED BY 10) pm EQUALS (k DIVIDED BY 10 AT MOST `the limit section 1ו sets for the track` t OR pm)
                                AND `the limit section 1ו sets for the track` t AT MOST `the limit section 1ו sets for the track` `a principal not employed under a reform`)
                            `both booleans`)
                    (range 0 20))
            `every track`

-- §2 over every share: exactly one band, the amount never falling (finding
-- e: the share in physical education decides).
#ASSERT all (GIVEN s YIELD
                    count (`the amounts the table gives for` s) EQUALS 1
                AND `the additional physical-education allowance` s AT MOST `the additional physical-education allowance` (s PLUS 0.1))
            `the shares checked`

-- §3 over every list of professions and every position: at most the
-- higher item, pro rata to the position up to one (finding d's reading).
#ASSERT all (GIVEN l YIELD
                all (GIVEN f YIELD
                        LET t MEANS `the technological-education allowance for the professions taught` l f
                        IN      t AT MOST 589 TIMES min f 1
                            AND count (`the items the lists give` l) AT MOST 2
                            AND t EQUALS (IF null (`the items the lists give` l) THEN 0 ELSE sum (take 1 (`the items the lists give` l)) TIMES min f 1))
                    `tenths to 1.5`)
            `every profession list checked`
